  "description": "Which sign got you? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend who checked all five. Mae skips the audition: there'll be other chances. In 'The Experience of Regret: What, When, and Why' (Psychological Review, 1995), Thomas Gilovich and Victoria Husted Medvec reviewed their studies of what people regret: in the short term, people regret the things they did more; looking back over the long term, they regret the things they didn't do. Mistakes fade. Missed chances stay. #psychology #shorts #regret #overthinking #confidence",
